<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Payment status">
        <FluentText>Every party shows one of these, worked out from what's been marked as paid:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" Color="BadgeColor.Warning">Unpaid</FluentBadge> Nothing has been paid yet.</li>
            <li><FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" Color="BadgeColor.Brand">Deposit paid</FluentBadge> The deposit is in; the balance is still to pay.</li>
            <li><FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" Color="BadgeColor.Success">Paid in full</FluentBadge> Nothing left to pay.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Recording payments">
        <ol>
            <li>Open the party. You can only record payments once it's been booked.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Payment</strong>, press <strong>Mark deposit paid</strong> when the deposit comes in, and
                <strong>Mark paid in full</strong> when the rest is paid. Lanyard records when each was marked and shows the balance still due.</li>
            <li>Marked one by mistake? Press <strong>Undo</strong> next to it.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Use <strong>Payment notes</strong> for how it was paid, for example by card over the phone. The deposit can't be more
            than the total price.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            <strong>Save changes</strong> never changes what's been paid, so someone editing a party that was open before the
            deposit came in can't undo it by saving.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Cancelling and reinstating">
        <FluentText>
            Open the party, press <strong>Cancel party</strong>, then <strong>Yes, cancel it</strong>. The party stays in Lanyard
            with a <FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Filled" Color="BadgeColor.Danger">Cancelled</FluentBadge> badge, and only
            appears on the list when <strong>Show cancelled</strong> is ticked. Press <strong>Reinstate party</strong> to put it back.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
